<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia cuts June crude palm oil export tax.</title>
<headline>Indonesia cuts June crude palm oil export tax.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia has reduced its export tax on crude palm oil to $39.20 a tonne in June from $47.32 in May, the finance ministry said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The tax on RBD palm olein was reduced to $55.30 a tonne in June from $68.60 while that on RBD palm oil was down to $42.64 in June from $53.04 in May, the ministry said. The tax on crude olein was reduced to $58.80 from $66.95.</p>
<p>The export taxes, introduced in September 1994, are based on a composite average of international prices in the last two weeks of the previous month and are aimed at ensuring sufficient supply and stable prices in the domestic market.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom + 6221 384-6364</p>
